# Island: a two-cell supercapacitor's balancing divider with a charge-limit resistor, and the 1 Mohm
# sense divider on the same 5 V rail. From a real 12 V automotive board: R27 and R26 (43k +/-1 %,
# row C8329), R28 (10 ohm, row C4346185), R30 and R29 (1M +/-1 %, row C26083) and the nets from the
# export of `netsmith build`. The rail is the board's 5 V..5.5 V; each cell leaks 0..6 uA (the
# board's own comment: "the cell's largest leakage (6 uA)"). The capacitor is an open circuit at DC.
# ASSUMPTION: the ADC pin does not drive (leakage 1 uA).
# report: v(MID) i(r27) i(r26) i(r28) p(r28) v(SENSE) i(r30)
# today: the divider's currents are stated by hand in the module (`balance_top.current == supply.voltage / (...)`); the cell voltages are not computed (a `balance_ratio` rule of thumb is checked instead)
V  rail   V5 GND 5..5.5
R  r27    V5 MID 43k+-1%
R  r26    MID BOT 43k+-1%
R  r28    BOT GND 10
I  leak_top  V5 MID 0..6u
I  leak_bot  MID BOT 0..6u
R  r30    V5 SENSE 1M+-1%
R  r29    SENSE GND 1M+-1%
L  adc    SENSE V3V3 GND states=Z rz=3.3M
V  v3v3   V3V3 GND 3.234..3.333
